# Build-context hygiene for the backend image.
#
# There was no ignore file, so `COPY . .` shipped the developer's virtualenv
# (614 MB of Python 3.14 packages), node_modules, caches and test output into
# the production image. The blocking Trivy scan caught it: the image's Python
# findings were the host venv's `wheel`/`urllib3`, not anything requirements.txt
# installs. Anything not needed at runtime stays out of the context.

# Local virtualenvs and their caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node (not part of this image)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets and local state must never be baked into a layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.tcdn-ai/

# VCS, editor and OS noise
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Tests, docs and local artefacts
tests/
docs/
*.md
!requirements.txt
*.log
*.sqlite3
*.db
